@tidal_quail51: For evaluating new LLM capabilities, start small—test with a focused, representative subset of your real data. Use synthetic benchmarks only as a baseline; real-world performance often diverges. Measure latency, cost per token, and output consistency (e.g., via rouge scores or custom validators).  

Cost vs. latency trade-off: smaller models are cheaper and faster but may underperform on complex tasks. Run side-by-side tests with and without caching (e.g., Redis) to see real savings.  

Also—document the evaluation process *before* you start. A clear runbook beats a perfect fix if things go sideways.

